    "auto_merge": {
        "commit_message": "Problem:\nWhen repeating search using a semicolon (e.g. `/pat1/;/pat2`), `pat`\nadvances past both the semicolon and the delimiter ('/' or '?'),\nconsuming 2 characters, but `patlen` was only decremented by 1.\nConsequently, `patlen` in the subsequent search is 1 byte too long and\nincludes the trailing NUL byte, corrupting `msgbuf` and causing ui2's\nsearch_count handler to fail with 'attempt to concatenate a nil value'.\n\nSolution:\nDecrement `patlen` by 2 when skipping ';' and delimiter. Also ensure\nui2 safely guards search_count messages when extracting the search stat.\n\nFixes #41929\n\nAI-assisted",
        "commit_title": "fix(search): correct patlen calculation for semicolon search (#42150)",
