    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen repeating search using a semicolon (e.g. `/pat1/;/pat2`), `pat` advances past both the semicolon and the delimiter ('/' or '?'), consuming 2 characters, but `patlen` was only decremented by 1. Consequently, `patlen` in the subsequent search is 1 byte too long and includes the trailing NUL byte, corrupting `msgbuf` and causing ui2's search_count handler to fail with 'attempt to concatenate a nil value'.\n\n### Solution\n\nDecrement `patlen` by 2 when skipping ';' and delimiter in `do_search()`. Also ensure ui2 safely guards search_count messages when extracting the search stat.\n\nFixes #41929",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-30T23:50:49Z",
